        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T14:40:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was going to suggest that there\u0027s a better name for this, based on the actual encoding type in the spec. That led me to re-discover a rabbit hole of Lab stuff, so I\u0027m not sure the math here is technically correct.\n\nFixed point Lab values use a different range, depending on which TAG they\u0027re in. Relevant paragraph from `10.10 lut16Type`:\n\n    For colour values that are in the PCSLAB colour space on the PCS side of\n    the tag, this tag uses the legacy 16-bit PCSLAB encoding defined in Tables\n    42 and 43, not the 16-bit PCSLAB encoding defined in 6.3.4.2. This encoding\n    is retained for backwards compatibility with profile version 2. The PCSLAB\n    L* values have a different encoding than the PCSLAB a* and PCSLAB b* values.\n    \nAh, wait - are we only using this to build PCSLAB values in an mAB or mBA tag? I\u0027m getting myself confused - the legacy encoding may only be for one-dimensional LUTs?",
      "revId": "0475fe5aa0a217419eb066810c3c32ee30dad857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "418449fa_c1f3a034",
        "filename": "src/core/SkICC.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 312,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-11T20:01:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is only for the grid_16 entry of skcms_A2B and skcms_B2A. I had been trying to find a more authoritative name, but this ended up feeling the best.\n\nThis math I pulled not from the spec, but from how skcms would interpret the CLUT. In particular:\n- Op_clut_A2B [0]\n  - this just divides the short value by 65535 [1]\n- Op_lab_to_xyz [2]\n  - and reverse operation at [3]\n\nThe spec definitely sounds that we should be using the legacy encoding here (where L\u003d1 should be encoded as 0xFF00, not 0xFFFF). Should I make a comment here indicating that this matches skcms and that the spec seems to indicate something slightly different?\n\n[0] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skcms/skcms.cc;l\u003d2752;drc\u003d8a9c775ac269415bd8a235b402562570189f8cfa\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h;l\u003d700;drc\u003d8a9c775ac269415bd8a235b402562570189f8cfa\n[2] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skcms/skcms.cc;l\u003d2787;drc\u003d8a9c775ac269415bd8a235b402562570189f8cfa\n[3] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/Transform_inl.h;l\u003d1198;drc\u003d8a9c775ac269415bd8a235b402562570189f8cfa",
      "parentUuid": "10cf3b88_804c81df",
      "revId": "0475fe5aa0a217419eb066810c3c32ee30dad857",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
